 or Portugal, you're in the one place where orcas and people keep colliding. Since May 2020, a small group of Iberian orcas has been circling sailboats and ramming their rudders. By recent counts, that's roughly seven hundred interactions, and by one estimate about a fifth of them left the boat disabled. The whole population is under forty animals, critically endangered since 2019, and only about fifteen of them are doing it. Fifteen animals, seven hundred encounters. Impressive work ethic.", "submitted_text": "If you sail off Spain or Portugal, you're in the one place where orcas and people keep colliding. Since May 2020, a small group of Iberian orcas has been circling sailboats and ramming their rudders. By recent counts, that's roughly seven hundred interactions, and by one estimate about a fifth of them left the boat disabled. The whole population is under forty animals, critically endangered since 2019, and only about fifteen of them are doing it. Fifteen animals, seven hundred encounters. Impressive work ethic.", "model_id": "eleven_v3", "voice_id": "bIHbv24MWmeRgasZH58o", "audio_bytes": 566795}